{
  "Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta Session Used from Multiple Countries",
  "Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access / T1539\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Session Used from Multiple Countries\" or \"<ip>|Okta Session Used from Multiple Countries\"\n\nOne Okta session (authenticationContext.rootSessionId) used from two or more countries within the search window, counting only computer-side events. Phone-side events (Okta Verify pushes over cellular networks) are excluded because they legitimately come from other networks. A session moving between countries within minutes suggests a stolen session cookie being replayed.\n\nFalse positives: VPN clients that switch exit countries mid-session.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_multiple_device_token_hashes_for_single_okta_session/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_multiple_device_token_hashes_for_single_okta_session.toml",
  "Labels": [
    "okta",
    "detection",
    "authentication-sessions",
    "credential-access",
    "T1539"
  ],
  "Schedule": "12,27,42,57 * * * *",
  "Duration": -900,
  "DefaultDeploymentRules": {
    "Disabled": false,
    "RunImmediately": false
